      "rationale": "The two tests target the two concretely-named regressed behaviours. The DoS-prevention test encodes the documented intent of MAX_GROUPING_TOKENS/MAX_GROUPING_DEPTH (per the CHANGELOG security-fix entry and AGENTS.md): they exist only to stop pathological/adversarial input, so a plain 5000-element IN(...) list - ordinary, legitimate SQL - must still parse without SQLParseError and must still be grouped into a proper IdentifierList inside the Parenthesis, exactly as it always did before the protection was added. The aligned-indent test encodes AlignedIndentFilter's documented column-alignment algorithm (api.rst + the filter's own nl()/`_process_identifierlist` logic, whose intended output for \"select a, b as bb, c from table\" aligns every subsequent column and the `from` clause's value under the first selected column), giving a fixed, unambiguous expected string derived from the documented/intended formatting rules rather than from whatever the current buggy code happens to emit.",
